# Live capture: VM/370 R6 (VM/CE 1.2) under Hercules, recorded 2026-08-17.
#
# Script: packages/cli/scripts/record-vm.txt (connect, LOGON CMSUSER, password,
# QUERY TERMINAL, LOGOFF). The host answered LOGOFF with its own timestamp, which
# is the proof our inbound stream is genuinely understood by CP.
#
# REDACTED: two records containing the account password have been replaced with
# comment lines -- one we sent, one the host echoed back. The fixture is therefore
# replay-faithful only up to the password prompt; screens after it reflect a
# session where the password bytes are absent. That is deliberate: a working
# password must never enter git history.
#
# Known quirks of this capture, not bugs:
#  - "DMKCFC001E ?CP: QUERY" is CP rejecting QUERY TERMINAL, which is a CMS
#    command, not a CP one. A scripting error in the original run, left as-is
#    because a rejected command is a perfectly good thing to have in a fixture.
#  - The session never reaches CMS; it stays at CP READ. Reaching CMS needs an
#    IPL, which this script does not do.
